[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2815971404","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105513#issuecomment-2815971404","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105513","id":2815971404,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6n2FBM","user":{"login":"Raftatul","id":80292778,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMjkyNzc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80292778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul","html_url":"https://github.com/Raftatul","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-18T18:20:32Z","updated_at":"2025-04-18T18:20:32Z","body":"> Tested locally, it works as expected.\r\n> \r\n> Note that setting this at startup will not defer controller initialization, so it won't sidestep #20566 on Windows. This is not critical to address the core need mentioned in [godotengine/godot-proposals#12259](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12259), but I thought I'd mention it regardless.\r\n> \r\n> This PR also doesn't implement a command line argument for games that don't expose an in-game option to toggle gamepad support. As mentioned in [godotengine/godot-proposals#12259 (comment)](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12259#issuecomment-2810815263), I'd like to have this as not all games will expose an option to disable gamepad support (especially smaller/gamejam projects).\r\n> \r\n> Lastly, controller vibration is not disabled when gamepad support is disabled. This should be done by adding an early `return` to `Input::start_joy_vibration()` and `Input::stop_joy_vibration()`.\r\n\r\nI’m not sure how to implement command lines yet, but I’ll look into it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2815971404/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2816034953","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105513#issuecomment-2816034953","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105513","id":2816034953,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6n2UiJ","user":{"login":"Raftatul","id":80292778,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMjkyNzc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80292778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul","html_url":"https://github.com/Raftatul","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-18T19:03:11Z","updated_at":"2025-04-18T19:03:11Z","body":"> Tested locally, it works as expected.\r\n> \r\n> Note that setting this at startup will not defer controller initialization, so it won't sidestep #20566 on Windows. This is not critical to address the core need mentioned in [godotengine/godot-proposals#12259](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12259), but I thought I'd mention it regardless.\r\n> \r\n> This PR also doesn't implement a command line argument for games that don't expose an in-game option to toggle gamepad support. As mentioned in [godotengine/godot-proposals#12259 (comment)](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12259#issuecomment-2810815263), I'd like to have this as not all games will expose an option to disable gamepad support (especially smaller/gamejam projects).\r\n> \r\n> Lastly, controller vibration is not disabled when gamepad support is disabled. This should be done by adding an early `return` to `Input::start_joy_vibration()` and `Input::stop_joy_vibration()`.\r\n\r\nOkay, I implemented the ``--disable-gamepad`` command line option and added the ``gamepad_enabled`` setting under ``input_devices/controller/gamepad_enabled`` in the project settings. I'm not sure if it's the right way to do it, though.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2816034953/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2817131579","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105513#issuecomment-2817131579","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105513","id":2817131579,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6n6gQ7","user":{"login":"MJacred","id":6639237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzkyMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6639237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred","html_url":"h