ount":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3974699373","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105513#issuecomment-3974699373","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105513","id":3974699373,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7s6Rlt","user":{"login":"Raftatul","id":80292778,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMjkyNzc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80292778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul","html_url":"https://github.com/Raftatul","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-27T19:31:03Z","updated_at":"2026-02-27T19:31:03Z","body":"> I would love to review this PR if @Nintorch's comments are addressed.\r\n> \r\n> One nitpick is that `joypad_enabled` refers to joypad as singular even though technically this API disables all joypad**s** (multiple). But this is not a hill I'd die on...\r\n\r\nIt’s been a long time since I worked on this PR. I will make the suggested changes today.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3974699373/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5085810947","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105513#issuecomment-5085810947","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105513","id":5085810947,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLyNRAw","user":{"login":"Raftatul","id":80292778,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMjkyNzc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80292778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul","html_url":"https://github.com/Raftatul","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-26T23:01:47Z","updated_at":"2026-07-26T23:01:47Z","body":"> Just tested this PR and found that if I disable joypad input while pushing a joystick to the side, then `Input.get_action_strength()` will keep returning the last value of the action instead of the expected value of `0`.\r\n> \r\n> Other than that, disabling joypads stops any events from propagating as far as I could see. Great!\r\n\r\nTo fix the `Input.get_action_strength()` bug, I'll need to modify `release_pressed_events`. This code is avoiding the input to be correctly released:\r\n```\r\nvoid Input::release_pressed_events() {\r\n\t// Don't release the events if the application (or the window it's embedded in) is still focused.\r\n\tif (application_focused || embedder_focused) {\r\n\t\treturn;\r\n\t}\r\n```\r\nI'm not sure why it's was added in the first place, I'll remove it for now. @Nintorch can you explain why did you added this? Was it to avoid some issues related to the controller?\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5085810947/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5086922895","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105513#issuecomment-5086922895","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105513","id":5086922895,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLzRIjw","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-27T03:17:50Z","updated_at":"2026-07-27T03:17:50Z","body":"Yes, if I remember correctly it was done so that controller events aren't released accidentally when the user switches focus between the editor (the \"embedder\") and the embedded game window","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5086922895/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5089895290","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105513#issuecomment-5089895290","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105513","id":5089895290,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABL2Gjeg","user":{"login":"Raftatul","id":80292778,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMjkyNzc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80292778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul","html_url":"https://github.com/Raftatul","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-27T09:55:24Z","updated_at":"2026-07-27T09:55:24Z","body":"> Yes, if I remember correctly it was done so that controller events aren't released accidentally when the user switches focus between the editor (the \"embedder\") and the embedded game window\n\nSo it's only an issue related to the editor? Is it still relevant? I could bypass the check by 