fic device input. It should work, but I can’t confirm it at 100% since I don’t have several controllers available. I'll also convert this PR to draft cause I think it's not completed yet.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5091401837/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5291792833","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105513#issuecomment-5291792833","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105513","id":5291792833,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABO2pZwQ","user":{"login":"AdriaandeJongh","id":5611323,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTEzMjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5611323?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh","html_url":"https://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-14T09:35:21Z","updated_at":"2026-08-14T09:35:21Z","body":"> I pushed something to disable a specific device input.\r\n\r\nThat could also be part of a separate PR, as to not delay the merging of this PR any further.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5291792833/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5987602377","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105513#issuecomment-5987602377","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105513","id":5987602377,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZOOPyQ","user":{"login":"AdriaandeJongh","id":5611323,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTEzMjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5611323?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh","html_url":"https://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-05T03:29:59Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T03:29:59Z","body":"> Although I'm not sure if it makes sense to return the joypads array in `Input.get_connected_joypads()` while every other method would not work with the values in the array.\r\n\r\ntricky question, thanks for asking. i think disabling the receiving of joypads events does not have to disable other functions of the joypad API per sé, but i understand what you are implying: if a game dev has disabled joypads, we can reasonably assume they expressly don’t care that one is connected and therefore ‘clean up’ any results from other joypad APIs, perhaps even to avoid any confusion… and with that i agree. so yes, perhaps other joypad API should start returning ‘nothing’ as if no controllers are connected.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5987602377/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5988226555","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105513#issuecomment-5988226555","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105513","id":5988226555,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZO0V-w","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-05T04:40:08Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T04:40:08Z","body":"I've just been reading https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/8391 and it mentions the \"capturing\" of a joypad by Godot, I assume this currently means that SDL in Godot sees the controller and exposes it?\n\nIf that's the case, then I think we might have to disable joypad support in a different way 😅 \n\nWe would have to prevent the joypad drivers (SDL, Android, and Web drivers) from working if the project setting is enabled. This would also remove a lot of code changes in `input.cpp` and it should disable controller support completely.\n\nWhat do you think?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5988226555/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5989581563","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105513#issuecomment-5989581563","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105513","id":5989581563,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZQHC-w","user":{"login":"AdriaandeJongh","id":5611323,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTEzMjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5611323?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh","html_url":"https://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-05T06:51:55Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T06:51:55Z","body":"This is precisely the kind of question that is out of my league as I don't know much about the implementation. The desired experience for game devs and players is that they want to be able to disable joypad input so that players aren't forced to disconnect their controllers and peripherals if those are sending input even though the player intends to use mouse & keyboard only.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5989581563/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]